sentences.t:
Ut me conspexit venientem et Troïa circum
arma amens vidit, magnis exterrita monstris
deriguit visu in medio, calor ossa reliquit;

sentences.l:
When she caught sight of me coming, and Trojan round about
arms, beside herself she saw them, by great portents terror-struck,
she froze in the midst of her gaze, the heat left her bones;

sentences.t:
pauca tibi e multis, quo tutior hospita lustres
aequora et Ausonio possis considere portu,
expediam dictis;

sentences.l:
a few things for you out of many, that more safely strange
seas you may traverse and in an Ausonian harbour be able to settle,
I shall set out in words;

sentences.t:
Has autem terras, Italique hanc litoris oram,
proxuma quae nostri perfunditur aequoris aestu,
effuge;

sentences.l:
But these lands, and this coast of the Italian shore,
which, nearest, is bathed by the tide of our sea,
flee;

sentences.t:
Hic et Narycii posuerunt moenia Locri,
et Sallentinos obsedit milite campos
Lyctius Idomeneus;

sentences.l:
Here also the Narycian Locrians have set their walls,
and the Sallentine plains has beset with soldiery
Lyctian Idomeneus;
